WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.080
One aim of Rethink Rubbish, is to see a lot
less stuff going in here

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.000
which all goes to landfill.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.120
When you do need to get rid of rubbish, here’s
what you need to know and the same rules apply

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.200
for both bins and official Council rubbish
bags.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.920
We can’t take hazardous or toxic waste,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.080
this includes stuff like engine oil and leftover paint.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:27.500
These should be taken to the Southbrook Resource
Recovery Park and disposed of properly

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.180
it’s usually free.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.960
We also can’t take explosives or ammunition,

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.980
ring your local police station for advice
when dealing with these.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.680
Broken glass or china should be well wrapped
with newspaper.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:44.660
And make sure ashes are completely cold before putting them in your bin or bag.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:54.680
To learn more or to sign up for collection
reminders visit waimakariri.govt.nz/rethinkrubbish

